    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on June 17, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) stands as our premier offensive anchor. Facing a favorable matchup against the left-handed Bennett (xERA 4.88), he benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP skill valuation and strong platoon indicators, making him a must-start in all formats. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.55) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.90) also grade out as elite options; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on the platoon advantage against the right-handed Avila, while **Drake Baldwin** finds himself in an ideal spot to exploit Whisenhunt\u2019s 5.46 xERA. These three represent the core of our daily efficiency goals, particularly as we hunt for counting stats in a favorable run-scoring environment.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the final utility spot, where **Miguel Vargas** (59.33) narrowly edged out **Brayan Rocchio** (53.93). While **Brayan Rocchio** has shown flashes, his lower base projection against a tougher matchup (Sproat) kept him on the bench. We also remain cautious with **Kyle Tucker** (59.41) and **Andy Pages** (58.48); despite facing the formidable McClanahan, both maintain marginal-to-strong viability due to their roles, though **Andy Pages** receives a marginal bump due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slower delivery speed, which theoretically opens a window for him to chip into our scarce stolen base needs.\n\nAs we look across the diamond, the primary risk remains the high-end talent of opposing arms like Kirby and McClanahan, who serve as a floor-reducer for even our strongest bats. **Nasim Nunez** (54.91) sits on the lower end of our starting threshold; while his speed is vital for the 5x5 category hunt, his placement in the nine-hole combined with the high-hold nature of the opposing pitcher makes him a volatile play. We are continuing to monitor the health of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined, placing additional pressure on our healthy outfielders like **Jackson Merrill** (67.78) and **Cole Carrigg** (65.20) to maximize their opportunities against their respective right-handed matchups.",
